From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: a station belongs to one node, enforced where it is linked
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

struct sta carries a single list head. Linking a station into a second node's
list without unlinking it from the first does not put it in two lists - it
splices the two lists together, and a walk over either never ends.

Measured on the live mesh 2026-09-06 14:55:

    95642 log lines in 32 seconds, ~3000 a second,
    from a collection whose timer fires once a second

The walk was not repeating. It was not returning. VSZ 20 MB -> 850 MB, ubus
stopped answering, no agent was processed for nine minutes, every node aged
past NODE_DRAW_MAX_AGE, and the entire topology vanished from the web UI.

Four call sites reach node_add_sta and each is expected to have detached the
station first. Three do it as

    old_n = cntlr_find_node(c, s->agent_almacaddr);
    if (old_n)
            node_del_sta(old_n, s);

and when that lookup misses, the detach is skipped while the add runs anyway.
Requiring four callers to remember is how this got here, so the rule is moved
to the one function that links.

The trigger needs no misbehaving client. One that moves ONCE leaves the old AP
holding a stale association - measured the same day, ba:a9:1b:53:17:82 idle
279 s on the node it had left while live on another - so two nodes report it,
which is the normal state during any handover.

Three changes, one idea: make "is this station attached?" answerable, and
answer it in the only place that attaches.

  node_add_sta       unlink and drop the earlier reference before linking
  node_del_sta       list_del_init, not list_del
  node_update_stalist  same

The _init matters. libubox list_del leaves the head {NULL, NULL}, so
list_empty() answers false for a station attached to nothing - the guard would
be blind from the first detach onwards - and a later list_del walks a NULL
pointer. Detached must look detached. sta_alloc() was missing its
INIT_LIST_HEAD for the same reason and is fixed in 99999995.

sta_dec_ref() does not free at zero; it starts the ageout timer, so the
station stays valid across the unlink.


--- a/src/cntlr.c
+++ b/src/cntlr.c
@@ -733,6 +733,42 @@
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+	/* A station is attached to AT MOST ONE node, and this is the only
+	 * place that attaches one - so this is where the rule is kept.
+	 *
+	 * struct sta carries a single list head. Linking it into a second
+	 * node's list without unlinking it from the first does not put it in
+	 * two lists; it splices the two lists together, and from then on a walk
+	 * over either of them never ends. Measured 2026-09-06: 95642 log lines
+	 * in 32 seconds from a collection whose timer fires once a second - the
+	 * walk was not repeating, it was not returning. VSZ 20 MB -> 850 MB,
+	 * ubus mute, no agent processed for nine minutes, and the whole
+	 * topology gone from the web UI.
+	 *
+	 * Four call sites reach this function and each one is expected to have
+	 * removed the station from its previous node first. Three of them do it
+	 * as "old_n = cntlr_find_node(...); if (old_n) node_del_sta(old_n, s);"
+	 * - and when that lookup misses, the removal is skipped while the add
+	 * below runs anyway. Requiring four callers to remember is how this got
+	 * here; the rule belongs in one place instead.
+	 *
+	 * The trigger needs no misbehaving client. One that moves ONCE leaves
+	 * the old AP holding a stale association - measured the same day,
+	 * ba:a9:1b:53:17:82 idle 279 s on the node it had left while live on
+	 * another - so two nodes report it, which is the normal state during
+	 * any handover.
+	 *
+	 * sta_dec_ref() balances the reference the earlier add took. It does
+	 * not free at zero, it starts the ageout timer, so s stays valid here.
+	 */
+	if (!list_empty(&s->list)) {
+		cntlr_warn(LOG_STA, "%s: STA " MACFMT " was still attached to a node"
+			   " - unlinking before adding to " MACFMT "\n",
+			   __func__, MAC2STR(s->macaddr), MAC2STR(n->almacaddr));
+		list_del_init(&s->list);
+		sta_dec_ref(s);
+	}
+
 	memcpy(s->agent_almacaddr, n->almacaddr, 6);
 	list_add(&s->list, &n->stalist);
 	n->sta_count++;
@@ -762,7 +798,12 @@
 			"\"bssid\":\"" MACFMT "\"}", MAC2STR(s->macaddr), MAC2STR(n->almacaddr), MAC2STR(s->bssid));
 	cntlr_notify_event(n->cntlr, CNTLR_EVENT_CLIENT_DISCONNECT, ev_data);
 
-	list_del(&s->list);
+	/* _init, not plain list_del: libubox's list_del leaves the head as
+	 * {NULL, NULL}, which makes list_empty() answer "false" for a station
+	 * attached to nothing - so the guard in node_add_sta would be blind
+	 * from the first detach onwards - and makes a later list_del walk a
+	 * NULL pointer. Detached must look detached. */
+	list_del_init(&s->list);
 	n->sta_count--;
 	sta_dec_ref(s);
 
@@ -796,7 +837,8 @@
 		}
 
 		if (!found) {
-			list_del(&s->list);
+			/* _init for the same reason as in node_del_sta. */
+			list_del_init(&s->list);
 			n->sta_count--;
 			sta_dec_ref(s);
 		}
